    <title>Case analysis of higher-order data
    </title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <h1>Abstract</h1>

<p>
  We discuss coverage checking for data that is dependently typed and
  is defined using higher-order abstract syntax.  Unlike previous work
  on coverage checking or closed data, we consider
  open data which may depend on some context.
  Our work may therefore provide insight into coverage checking in
  Twelf, and serve as a basis for coverage checking in functional
  languages such as Delphin and Beluga. More generally, our work is a
  foundation for proofs by case analysis in systems that reason about
  higher-order abstract syntax.
</p>

